guilty|responsible-for-wrongdoing|ADJECTIVE|Responsible for wrongdoing|Responsible for committing a crime or doing something wrong.|có tội; mắc lỗi|In the story, the investigation proves that the guard is guilty of theft.|Trong câu chuyện, cuộc điều tra chứng minh rằng người bảo vệ có tội trộm cắp.|Guilty of plus noun or -ing; found guilty. This word describes responsibility, distinct from merely feeling guilty.|0
guilty|feeling-remorse|ADJECTIVE|Feeling remorse|Feeling bad because one believes one has done something wrong or neglected a responsibility.|áy náy; cảm thấy có lỗi|She felt guilty about forgetting her friend's birthday.|Cô ấy thấy có lỗi vì quên sinh nhật của bạn mình.|Feel guilty about something or for doing something. A feeling alone does not prove actual wrongdoing.|1
million|one-thousand-thousand|NUMBER|One thousand thousand|The number 1,000,000.|triệu|The exhibition attracted more than a million visitors over several years.|Triển lãm thu hút hơn một triệu lượt khách trong vài năm.|One million, two million without plural -s after a number; millions of for an unspecified large quantity.|0
portion|part-of-a-whole|NOUN|Part of a whole|An amount or section separated from, or belonging to, something larger.|phần; phần được chia|Each visitor received a small portion of the cake.|Mỗi khách nhận một phần bánh nhỏ.|Countable; a portion of something, a generous portion. Commonly used for a serving of food.|0
sentence|grammatical-unit|NOUN|Grammatical unit|A group of words that expresses a statement, question or command as a grammatical whole.|câu|The teacher asked us to write one sentence describing the picture.|Giáo viên yêu cầu chúng tôi viết một câu miêu tả bức tranh.|Countable; write a sentence. In writing, a sentence normally begins with a capital and ends with appropriate punctuation.|0
sentence|impose-a-punishment|VERB|Impose a punishment|To officially decide what punishment a convicted person must receive.|tuyên án; kết án|In the fictional trial, the judge sentenced the defendant to two years in prison.|Trong phiên tòa hư cấu, thẩm phán tuyên án bị cáo hai năm tù.|Sentence someone to a punishment; often passive, be sentenced to. Sentenced and sentencing are regular forms.|1
sentence|official-punishment|NOUN|Official punishment|A punishment formally given to a person found guilty of a crime.|bản án; hình phạt được tuyên|The character appealed against the sentence in the novel.|Nhân vật kháng cáo bản án trong tiểu thuyết.|Countable; receive a sentence, serve a prison sentence. The grammatical-unit noun is a separate meaning.|2
worthwhile|worth-the-effort|ADJECTIVE|Worth the effort|Useful or valuable enough to justify the time, effort or money involved.|đáng công; đáng giá|Repairing the old desk was worthwhile because it fitted the room perfectly.|Việc sửa chiếc bàn cũ đáng công vì nó rất vừa với căn phòng.|A worthwhile activity; it is worthwhile doing or to do something. Different from worth, which usually takes a noun or -ing.|0
